config MPIPE_IPC
	bool "Direct inter-core IPC protocol"
	select CRC
	help
	  Version 1 wire protocol for the direct M7 to HiFi4 link: framing,
	  CRC32C integrity, structural validation, and the paired session
	  state machine. Transport independent; it marshals bytes and decides
	  whether they are currently meaningful, while the IPC Service backend
	  moves them between cores.

config MPIPE_IPC_PLUGIN
	bool "Cross-core pipeline elements"
	depends on MPIPE_IPC && IPC_SERVICE
	help
	  Build the IPC sink and source elements, which let one pipeline span
	  two cores: it ends on one in an IPC sink and resumes on the other in
	  an IPC source. Buffers cross by reference, so the pool the sink draws
	  from must live in memory the peer can address.
